[2026-08-04T11:35:34.478Z] [INFO] [client] MCP tool call request, session=1i40jlMDRuVugR55qEJ40GVV6PQ6wiQjlIBZfah9vWy8NiYY0QRPSwFX4IyI, tool=create_pull_request, args={"body":"Updates the \"Histograms in delta temporality only\" limitation, which was outdated as a blanket statement. Both `delta` and `cumulative` temporality are now supported for histogram and counter metrics when ingesting data through the Managed OTLP endpoint (Stack 9.5+, already GA on serverless). The `delta`-only restriction is scoped down to apply only to the collector Elasticsearch exporter path, which does not yet support cumulative temporality for histograms.\n\n**Triage rationale**: Issue #648 provided a clear, verifiable, and scoped documentation request — specific file, specific lines, exact product behavior change, and version applicability. The claim was independently verified against the published [Metric temporality](https://www.elastic.co/docs/manage-data/ingest/otlp-endpoint#metric-temporality) documentation, which confirms cumulative and delta temporality support via the OTLP endpoint and the `xpack.otel_data.histogram_field_type` requirement. No conflicting evidence was found.\n\n**Drafting sources**\n- `/docs/contribute-docs` and cumulative-docs `applies_to` guidance (repository conventions, since the MCP docs server tools were unavailable in this run; version-tag syntax cross-checked against existing `applies_to` usage in `docs/reference/index.md`)\n- Published doc: [Metric temporality](https://www.elastic.co/docs/manage-data/ingest/otlp-endpoint#metric-temporality)\n- Issue #648 body (implementation evidence and caveats)\n\n**Reader test**\n- Reader goal: understand whether cumulative temporality is supported for histogram/counter metrics and under what conditions.\n- Rounds: 2. Round 1 flagged ambiguity about whether the collector-exporter limitation also applied to counters and whether it overlapped with the OTLP endpoint path. Round 2 fix added an explicit sentence scoping the collector-exporter limitation to `Histogram` metrics only, separate from the OTLP endpoint path. No blocking gaps remained after the fix.\n\nRelated to #648\n\nThis draft PR was produced autonomously by docs-agent-experimental in experimental mode.\n\nSafe-output PRs do not trigger CI by default. A maintainer must trigger the required checks manually.","title":"Update histogram/counter temporality limitation for the Managed OTLP endpoint (9.5+ / serverless)"}
